import tests/games/studio/viewport.dl
import tests/games/gallery/interface.dl

to paint the gallery on {a pointer to UI canvas frame:canvas}:
    set session to the gallery in (canvas's instance)
    set view to session's view as a pointer to native UI view
    set frame to canvas's frame
    set box to the framebuffer box of (canvas's bounds) in view
    set session's bounds to canvas's bounds
    use viewport box on frame
    use (the item at (session's selected) in (session's programs)) in frame
    set uniform binding 0 in frame to session's elapsed
    set uniform binding 1 in frame to box's width
    set uniform binding 2 in frame to box's height
    set uniform binding 3 in frame to box's x
    set uniform binding 4 in frame to box's y
    set cursor to the UI cursor in view
    set {mouse x} to the maximum of 0.0 and (the minimum of (canvas's bounds' width) and (cursor's x - canvas's bounds' x))
    set {mouse y} to the maximum of 0.0 and (the minimum of (canvas's bounds' height) and (cursor's y - canvas's bounds' y))
    set uniform binding 5 in frame to mouse x * box's width / canvas's bounds' width
    set uniform binding 6 in frame to mouse y * box's height / canvas's bounds' height
    set uniform binding 7 in frame to session's elapsed - session's pulse
    set uniform binding 8 in frame to session's camera x
    set uniform binding 9 in frame to session's camera y
    draw a fullscreen surface in frame
    restore the viewport on frame

